### Handling Shell Execution
For commands that need to pass raw shell strings (supporting pipes `|` and redirects `>`), you should use the direct execution pattern.
Standard Go `exec` arguments are escaped, which breaks these features. To fix this, reconstruct the command string and pass it to `sh -c`.

```go
var shellCmd = &cobra.Command{
  Use:   "shell [cmd]",
  Short: "Execute a shell command",
  Run: func(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) {
    // Construct the full command string from arguments
    // Note: To support wildcards and pipes, we must NOT sanitize the input.
    // Sanitization will escape the operators and break the functionality.
    fullCommand := strings.Join(args, " ")
    c := exec.Command("sh", "-c", fullCommand)
    c.Stdout = os.Stdout
    c.Stderr = os.Stderr
    c.Run()
  },
}
```

